From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 12:49:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02576/11362] [outer-loop] richer dynamics (growth agent) +
 disambiguation (cell-based heuristic): sound, no regression, but cd82/m0r0
 need MORE

Built both requested agent-model improvements:
  (1) RICHER DYNAMICS -- identify_agent_rich: rigid TRANSLATION first; if none, a GROWTH/shrink agent
      (_growth_agent: the colour whose cell-count changes incrementally under actions). Paired with
      _agent_centroid's largest-component fallback so a growing object is tracked.
  (2) DISAMBIGUATION -- agent_to_color_dist + induce_goal_color rewritten CELL-based (min manhattan
      from any agent-colour cell to any goal cell) instead of a single centroid, so they are robust to
      (a) growth agents whose centroid drifts and (b) multiple same-colour agent instances (m0r0).

RESULT (no banked solve):
  NO REGRESSION: all 5 prior solves hold -- sp80/cn04/ar25/tu93/ls20 (4/14/15/18/13 actions).
  cd82: richer-dynamics ID now SUCCEEDS (identifies the colour-4 GROWTH agent where translation-only
        returned None) -- but the win is no longer stumbled: a growth agent's centroid makes a WORSE
        exploration key than the grid-hash fallback. cd82 needs growth-appropriate EXPLORATION, not
        just growth ID -- a further, separate gap.
  m0r0: unchanged (not stumbled) -- its blocker is exploration depth, which disambiguation does not
        address.

HONEST META-CONCLUSION: the changes are correct and improve robustness with no regression, but they
do NOT unlock the two target games -- each has FURTHER idiosyncratic structure (growth-exploration,
exploration-depth). This is the long-tail of ARC-AGI-3: chasing the remaining games one mechanic at a
time is the GameAdapter anti-pattern, not convergence on a general solver. The solver holds at 5/10
first-contact with a fully-measured failure map. Adversarial-verify: clean.

